#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114865 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34b7ab4-a17b-5667-bd2b-5ed53e43afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "5adf056c-d122-54e6-b55f-5e85d39750c4" :question/math-academy-id "e-207" :question/problem "Calculate $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ if $y = 2 \\,\\textrm {arccot } x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccot } x) \t=  -\\dfrac 1 {1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\,\\text{arccot }x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccot }x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114869 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20a5f15e-8a26-57af-a867-8f8ae02a91c1" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "99db3f5c-5d6f-5e8e-a31c-a627ddd5c6dc" :question/math-academy-id "e-208" :question/problem "If $f(x) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{arcsec } x}{\\textrm{arccsc } x},$ calculate $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we let $u(x) = \\textrm{arcsec } x$ and $v(x) = \\textrm{arccsc } x$, and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\nu'(x) =  \\dfrac 1 {|x| \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}}\t\\quad \\text{and} \\quad\tv'(x) = -\\dfrac 1 {|x| \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\text{arccsc }x-\\text{arcsec }x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})}{{\\text{arccsc }}^{2}x} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})\\frac{\\text{arccsc }x+\\text{arcsec }x}{{\\text{arccsc }}^{2}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arccsc }x+\\text{arcsec }x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}{\\text{ arccsc }}^{2}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114872 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "905d1f6a-72aa-5984-8c7d-920497fd58e4" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "fd6239d1-4fec-50b9-8018-f6e185c4e0d0" :question/math-academy-id "e-209" :question/problem "If $f(x) =3 x\\, \\textrm {arccsc }x,$ calculate $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccsc}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccsc } x) \t=  -\\dfrac 1 {|x| \\sqrt {x^2 - 1}} \\, .\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x\\,\\text{arccsc }x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\,\\text{arccsc }x) \\\\  & =3(x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccsc }x)+\\text{arccsc }x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)) \\\\  & =3x(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})+3\\,\\text{arccsc }x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+3\\,\\text{arccsc }x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114874 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c1def23-83e0-5dc7-b20b-9693127d3a9e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "38c9e8d8-871f-54b1-a8df-637f54430cc1" :question/math-academy-id "e-210" :question/problem "Find $f'(x)$ if $f(x) =2 \\, \\textrm {arccot } (x^2 + 5).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\textrm{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}(\\textrm {arccot } x) \t=  -\\dfrac 1 {1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\,\\text{arccot }({x}^{2}+5)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1+({x}^{2}+5)^{2}})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+5) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{1+({x}^{2}+5)^{2}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4x}{1+({x}^{2}+5)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4x}{{x}^{4}+10{x}^{2}+26}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282707 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34b7ab4-a17b-5667-bd2b-5ed53e43afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0903c05c-41d5-5ea5-bc07-c2e58209ba78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282709} {:answer/id #uuid "ca1458e3-ebaf-5995-9066-283fa8ab4a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282710} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c36791-6a2f-51e7-9939-4c1f16661326" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282711} {:answer/id #uuid "4df82702-7f99-5e04-932d-c46d9bf06dbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282712} {:answer/id #uuid "a4975d8b-b25f-5450-b585-2b5d77c1bb2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0903c05c-41d5-5ea5-bc07-c2e58209ba78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282709} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fab36b2-1a55-5b6c-85ad-d911ac46f1bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da33d32a-51d8-587d-b45c-abd810d5a74c" :question/math-academy-id "q-110510" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=-7arccscx$ at $x=\\sqrt{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arccsc$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-7arccscx) \\\\  & =-7\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\sqrt{5}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\sqrt{5}) & =\\frac{7}{|\\sqrt{5}|\\sqrt{{\\sqrt{5}}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{5}\\sqrt{5-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282714 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34b7ab4-a17b-5667-bd2b-5ed53e43afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38ac6303-4057-50c7-955c-9d29654de747" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282716} {:answer/id #uuid "5c311ed6-ac18-5d12-9aac-9c128194d849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282717} {:answer/id #uuid "2a950ffa-dda7-5c9f-ab89-b2def2e02865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x}}+\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282718} {:answer/id #uuid "8f5ae844-7c6c-5cbd-a10e-e44fcbada0cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282719} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a32ec2-0680-5b27-89e8-54891804a15d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1a32ec2-0680-5b27-89e8-54891804a15d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282720} :answer-field/id #uuid "03666427-8f41-5df3-a2e7-8144cb490431" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "abdda85f-6c0c-52ca-ad4f-c1d33010c7d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-110517" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=2\\sqrt{x}+5arccscx.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arccsc$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\sqrt{x}+5arccscx) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+5\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+5(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20a5f15e-8a26-57af-a867-8f8ae02a91c1" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "123b58ad-f095-5d74-b122-704a178062ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{2}-4(1+{x}^{2})arccotx}{{x}^{4}(1+{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282723} {:answer/id #uuid "2d590417-8016-556f-bd37-e1639f9cbd2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+3{x}^{2}arccotx}{{x}^{4}(1-{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282724} {:answer/id #uuid "3c4c26bc-e296-581c-ac56-8d2d4826174b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-(1+{x}^{2})arccotx}{{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282725} {:answer/id #uuid "7761399a-a213-5bf0-b5e9-ae6dbf8dd076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+3(1+{x}^{2})arccotx}{{x}^{4}(1+{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282726} {:answer/id #uuid "940fdeda-24af-51f1-b035-05ccff627e37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x+3(1+{x}^{2}){x}^{2}arccotx}{{x}^{4}(1+{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7761399a-a213-5bf0-b5e9-ae6dbf8dd076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+3(1+{x}^{2})arccotx}{{x}^{4}(1+{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282726} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a796016-e711-5066-9c3a-5ddc3c0884e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35da99b2-e525-5a87-bbeb-6057eba4054b" :question/math-academy-id "q-110786" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{arccotx}{{x}^{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we let $u(x)=arccotx$ and $v(x)={x}^{3},$ and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{and}\\,{v}^{′}(x)=3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\cdot {x}^{3}-arccotx\\cdot 3{x}^{2}}{({x}^{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{1+{x}^{2}}-3{x}^{2}arccotx}{{x}^{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{3}+3(1+{x}^{2}){x}^{2}arccotx}{1+{x}^{2}})}{{x}^{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{3}+3(1+{x}^{2}){x}^{2}arccotx}{{x}^{6}(1+{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{x+3(1+{x}^{2})arccotx}{{x}^{4}(1+{x}^{2})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282728 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "905d1f6a-72aa-5984-8c7d-920497fd58e4" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4627ee59-be2d-51bc-8acf-fdd08c4f3d92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "arccsc{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282730} {:answer/id #uuid "64e0ec7d-6f3c-51f0-a566-df771f706d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "arccscx\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282731} {:answer/id #uuid "f2f095f8-1e8f-5fd2-b002-29d8ac5848ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "arccsc{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282732} {:answer/id #uuid "f631a670-af8e-5ad5-83db-dd820164af59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "arccsc{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282733} {:answer/id #uuid "63fcf52b-e205-532e-b0bb-dbeec1b3daa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "arccscx\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f631a670-af8e-5ad5-83db-dd820164af59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "arccsc{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282733} :answer-field/id #uuid "589887ee-43a6-56c7-a15c-f1705f5a5478" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f96882ab-e18d-5ec0-92db-ae32aa8216d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-110791" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot arccsc{x}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arccsc$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccsc{x}^{2}) & =-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccsc{x}^{2})+arccsc{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}})+arccsc{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =arccsc{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282735 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "905d1f6a-72aa-5984-8c7d-920497fd58e4" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de3e58ef-55a7-59b5-9343-35063e020006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{arccot3{x}^{2}}{x}-\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{1+{x}^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282737} {:answer/id #uuid "ca61c379-b42a-556c-808b-767267af91e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{arccot{x}^{3}}{x}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{1+{x}^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282738} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a2fb07-eb33-516a-aa15-63507d82cad6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{arccot{x}^{3}}{x}-\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{1-{x}^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282739} {:answer/id #uuid "03aeea1e-4837-5267-a400-99f6b31654d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{arccot{x}^{3}}{x}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{1-{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282740} {:answer/id #uuid "b540f889-ac93-5a5b-b449-8f605a72eec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{arccot3{x}^{2}}{x}-\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{1+{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca61c379-b42a-556c-808b-767267af91e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{arccot{x}^{3}}{x}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{1+{x}^{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282738} :answer-field/id #uuid "d340a2fe-05f5-5dcc-b168-8548ccf5d51c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "48740a36-951e-5602-94b1-6e787cb30868" :question/math-academy-id "q-110817" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡xarccot{x}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\text{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccotx)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, the formula above and the chain rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡xarccot{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot{x}^{3})+arccot{x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{1+{({x}^{3})}^{2}})+arccot{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{arccot{x}^{3}}{x}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{1+{x}^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282742 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20a5f15e-8a26-57af-a867-8f8ae02a91c1" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c0084b5-3147-50ef-b0a3-680f47ad1a67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+4}{arccscx}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282744} {:answer/id #uuid "6e8b1548-a5f1-5c1c-9ec3-4ec676db652c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+4}{arccscx}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282745} {:answer/id #uuid "89120c3b-e6e1-5bd9-b6de-980f0d915541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{arccscx}-\\frac{2x+4x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282746} {:answer/id #uuid "95e68409-b254-5dbe-805a-3ac1fdf7dc91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x+2}{arcsecx}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282747} {:answer/id #uuid "373bea4e-6466-59f7-a53e-9428c9d23497" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+4}{arccscx}-\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e8b1548-a5f1-5c1c-9ec3-4ec676db652c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+4}{arccscx}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282745} :answer-field/id #uuid "e65d2b9e-6021-519a-bae0-a0fcd1cd4f89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10ef82b2-bd9d-5fd0-8d9d-21fd5cdbf4b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-110834" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{arccscx}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we let $u(x)={x}^{2}+4x$ and $v(x)=arccscx,$ and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2x+4\\,\\text{and}\\,{v}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+4)\\cdot arccscx-({x}^{2}+4x)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})}{{arccsc}^{2}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+4}{arccscx}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "905d1f6a-72aa-5984-8c7d-920497fd58e4" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22a7d29f-2810-5e63-848e-f1c021da56d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "arccotx-\\frac{({x}^{3}+2x)(3{x}^{2}+2)}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282751} {:answer/id #uuid "c8962ad7-df43-520f-a3b2-00bdc031bfc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3{x}^{2}+2)-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282752} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2faed0-a97c-5c3b-bd9b-f7bdc660d8bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3{x}^{2}+2)arccotx-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282753} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc6737b-83f2-58ab-9a91-d450bc89e653" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "arccotx-\\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282754} {:answer/id #uuid "88e434a0-4e93-54b4-9fbf-3125ab73bf9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3{x}^{2}+2)arccotx-\\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88e434a0-4e93-54b4-9fbf-3125ab73bf9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3{x}^{2}+2)arccotx-\\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282755} :answer-field/id #uuid "58cc4ce9-9df6-510e-879b-627e31a81e02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a183af2-b9c0-56b5-8608-49e8ddb137c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-19065" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=({x}^{3}+2x)arccotx.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccotx)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(({x}^{3}+2x)arccotx) \\\\  & =arccotx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}+2x)+({x}^{3}+2x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccotx) \\\\  & =arccotx\\cdot (3{x}^{2}+2)+({x}^{3}+2x)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}+2)arccotx-\\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "905d1f6a-72aa-5984-8c7d-920497fd58e4" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "976b9f42-f485-5d58-9410-f1a023309122" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2arccscx}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282758} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e2fe74-45db-5404-bce1-046f80a8c806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2arcsecx}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282759} {:answer/id #uuid "b2068ba1-18b5-534d-bae3-d544e4ebf42f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282760} {:answer/id #uuid "0164d8b3-80ed-5bfa-9397-143c50d659d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{arccscx-arcsecx}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282761} {:answer/id #uuid "4feb6c98-d473-583a-be48-77b3b134ba8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{arccscx+arcsecx}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0164d8b3-80ed-5bfa-9397-143c50d659d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{arccscx-arcsecx}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282761} :answer-field/id #uuid "3af2a650-8d0d-523b-9b33-32db22adbd9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "71e5c02b-fbcb-5a16-a48a-593db81fecae" :question/math-academy-id "q-2484" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=arccscx\\cdot arcsecx$" :question/worked-solution "The formulae for the derivatives of $arccsc$ and $arcsec$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx) & =-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsecx) & =\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formulae above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =arcsecx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx)+arccscx\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsecx) \\\\  & =arcsecx\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})+arccscx\\cdot (\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{arcsecx}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+\\frac{arccscx}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{arccscx-arcsecx}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282763 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34b7ab4-a17b-5667-bd2b-5ed53e43afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ae3fe3f-90e2-5d1f-b49d-f6e0f7f04581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+1}{x^2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282765} {:answer/id #uuid "4c4cb26f-4faf-5f42-aede-c20ecd6b6285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x-1}{x^2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c4cb26f-4faf-5f42-aede-c20ecd6b6285" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x-1}{x^2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282766} :answer-field/id #uuid "1972dc8c-14ea-555b-9cf8-33d9302563e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5464cff0-d612-51e8-ae1f-a287bd88ea84" :question/math-academy-id "q-312358" :question/problem "If $f(x)=\\text{arccot }x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1),$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\text{arccot}$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccot }x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccot }x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282767 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c1def23-83e0-5dc7-b20b-9693127d3a9e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "350c092d-4234-56ec-ab00-800ff7788965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "350c092d-4234-56ec-ab00-800ff7788965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282769} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3f74186-85b1-5183-9df9-84e2d580d377" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e500b98d-716a-56c2-928c-2a1ac540ae13" :question/math-academy-id "q-312364" :question/problem "Calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=5arcsec({x}^{2}+3)$ at $x=2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arcsec$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsec\\,x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5arcsec({x}^{2}+3)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}+3|\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+3)^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+3) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}+3|\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+3)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{10x}{|{x}^{2}+3|\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+3)^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{10(2)}{|{2}^{2}+3|\\sqrt{({2}^{2}+3)^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{|7|\\sqrt{49-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{7\\sqrt{48}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{7\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282770 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20a5f15e-8a26-57af-a867-8f8ae02a91c1" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71f7bfdf-b9fb-531b-80e2-6f90c8d0736f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71f7bfdf-b9fb-531b-80e2-6f90c8d0736f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282772} :answer-field/id #uuid "071cc1af-1be6-5239-a884-2264b02d748e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282771} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b364be9f-8142-5097-a442-61cd5527a795" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2+5}{\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b364be9f-8142-5097-a442-61cd5527a795" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2+5}{\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282774} :answer-field/id #uuid "80ae2a14-216d-5daf-b4f4-ab1a5bcf3093" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f287a5e1-90d1-51aa-b84d-a524d5dafda5" :question/math-academy-id "q-312391" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+5}{arcsec\\,x}.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} \n$\\frac{1}{arcsec\\,x}\\,-$\n\n{{field-2}} \n$\\frac{1}{|x|{arcsec}^{2}\\,x}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we let $u(x)={x}^{2}+5$ and $v(x)=arcsec\\,x,$ and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2x\\,\\text{and}\\,{v}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x)\\cdot arcsec\\,x-({x}^{2}+5)\\cdot \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}}{(arcsec\\,x)^{2}}. \\\\  & =2x\\,\\frac{1}{arcsec\\,x}-\\frac{{x}^{2}+5}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\frac{1}{|x|{arcsec}^{2}\\,x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c1def23-83e0-5dc7-b20b-9693127d3a9e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c686ec97-5077-5aa6-b0f8-d2b68102ff60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282777} {:answer/id #uuid "2d8e59a2-767f-5ce6-b711-00d93397ddd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282778} {:answer/id #uuid "1f949076-9024-5950-b2c4-a5562da7a51f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282779} {:answer/id #uuid "3106f6e3-60e8-5a25-8e25-eb6164164c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282780} {:answer/id #uuid "77eedea7-91cb-5e52-8d4f-6c45c93fd3cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f949076-9024-5950-b2c4-a5562da7a51f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282779} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a2ddca2-3b60-567b-aeaf-4e721f1f3668" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d31c3cb9-e04d-585e-b687-400e1b6c482d" :question/math-academy-id "q-31903" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent line to the function $y=arcsec({x}^{3}-6x)$ at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arcsec$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsecx)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsec({x}^{3}-6x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}-6x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}-6}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line to the curve at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(1)\\text{ } & =\\frac{3(1)^{2}-6}{|{1}^{3}-6(1)|\\sqrt{({1}^{3}-6(1))^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{|-5|\\sqrt{(1-6)^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{4\\cdot 6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\cdot \\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\cdot 2\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{10\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{10\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{60} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115658 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c1def23-83e0-5dc7-b20b-9693127d3a9e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81fb3181-a375-50f9-b135-f88ec9ed023d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (12x^{3})/(\\mid 8 - x^{4} \\mid \\sqrt{(8 - x^{4})^{2} - 1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113349} {:answer/id #uuid "8e1c5933-a0f2-5eb9-8d7e-e39f572f7e32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x^{3})/(\\mid 8 - x^{4} \\mid \\sqrt{(8 - x^{4})^{2} - 1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113350} {:answer/id #uuid "9662b8a9-ed16-56fb-9248-bff8e449793f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8x^{3})/(\\mid 8 - x^{4} \\mid \\sqrt{(8 - x^{4})^{2} - 1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113351} {:answer/id #uuid "a27bd45b-dc88-5851-8b6a-8514851cc390" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12x^{3})/(\\mid 8 - x^{4} \\mid \\sqrt{(8 - x^{4})^{2} - 1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113352} {:answer/id #uuid "fb75b4b0-097a-5b28-a7a5-c0d805348b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (4x^{3})/(\\mid 8 - x^{4} \\mid \\sqrt{(8 - x^{4})^{2} - 1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9662b8a9-ed16-56fb-9248-bff8e449793f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8x^{3})/(\\mid 8 - x^{4} \\mid \\sqrt{(8 - x^{4})^{2} - 1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113351} :answer-field/id #uuid "24425df8-75e4-5fb6-a1e7-c2922dde3148" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5f8a50f-d033-5259-86d9-bade982764d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-32000" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=2arccsc(8-{x}^{4}).$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\text{arccsc}$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\text{arccsc}\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2arccsc(8-{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccsc(8-{x}^{4})) \\\\  & =2(-\\frac{1}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8-{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =2(-\\frac{1}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}})\\cdot (-4{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{|8-{x}^{4}|\\sqrt{(8-{x}^{4})^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34b7ab4-a17b-5667-bd2b-5ed53e43afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2a155fc-0343-563e-b60f-9fed602cadb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2a155fc-0343-563e-b60f-9fed602cadb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282784} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fbed088-7d60-5ba1-a3f4-ecc19433c0ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2839017f-d36a-5dd4-be44-dad05c9ac75a" :question/math-academy-id "q-341104" :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y=2x+arccotx$ at $x=0.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+arccotx) \\\\  & =2+(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={y}^{′}(0) & =2-\\frac{1}{1+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282785 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c1def23-83e0-5dc7-b20b-9693127d3a9e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8006bc8-61ae-5cff-ad21-3760811f64a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282787} {:answer/id #uuid "452aa4c2-874a-518e-8282-5ccc17e5e644" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "452aa4c2-874a-518e-8282-5ccc17e5e644" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282788} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2b61ab3-8ba0-55c1-b35b-b8683e368a6f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cdb30687-9cf3-58a5-bd82-f54a25ec0566" :question/math-academy-id "q-341115" :question/problem "Calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=arcsec({e}^{x})$ at $x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡10.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arcsec$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsec\\,x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[arcsec({e}^{x})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{e}^{x}|\\sqrt{{({e}^{x})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡10$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡10) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(10)/2)}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c1def23-83e0-5dc7-b20b-9693127d3a9e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4171c1c-bee9-55e1-a978-d1ef0391896b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4171c1c-bee9-55e1-a978-d1ef0391896b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282791} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b131200-d08a-527d-b1fc-fb96db18a88e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7baa460e-75bc-5492-9c26-cad5bfa18a98" :question/math-academy-id "q-341121" :question/problem "Calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=arccsc(\\sqrt{x})$ at $x=2.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arccsc$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccsc\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[arccsc(\\sqrt{x})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|\\sqrt{x}|\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{x-1}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{x-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(2) & =-\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2-1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "905d1f6a-72aa-5984-8c7d-920497fd58e4" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a3c17a6-dd98-5816-83d3-9445394840ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^x}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a3c17a6-dd98-5816-83d3-9445394840ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e^x}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282794} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a475c59-8abb-525b-be82-2553aa8cc4af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282793}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "624e21b1-55f1-5ea7-a70e-9b4efbbbc1ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-341146" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={e}^{x}\\cdot arccot\\,x.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}\\,arccot\\,x\\,-$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}\\cdot arccot\\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})\\cdot arccot\\,x+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,arccot\\,x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,arccot\\,x-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282795 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34b7ab4-a17b-5667-bd2b-5ed53e43afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e28fe70-e4e9-5da1-9e9f-d66ecb488025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282797} {:answer/id #uuid "16f8d824-57e5-5c85-80d6-a5de96566cea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282798} {:answer/id #uuid "564d4e18-cf74-5b1e-9286-64abccaf7bc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{2|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282799} {:answer/id #uuid "d08ec880-179a-5de9-abb6-5f8e3ead7642" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282800} {:answer/id #uuid "b302d456-9f7b-5932-878c-7a4fbc440f87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b302d456-9f7b-5932-878c-7a4fbc440f87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282801} :answer-field/id #uuid "03712dd9-5a48-5a76-9fae-c5a0f6b64b84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db5ccbbb-ec3b-5ab8-949d-761587ac2154" :question/math-academy-id "q-73437" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}-2arccscx.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $arccsc$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}-2arccscx) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-2(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{2}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282802 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20a5f15e-8a26-57af-a867-8f8ae02a91c1" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8642d0a1-2566-5d24-88b4-bbedd299fb99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1+{x}^{2}arccotx}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282804} {:answer/id #uuid "59c8c876-3df0-5ae5-8f0f-2934903b1a53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+(1+{x}^{2})arccotx}{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282805} {:answer/id #uuid "856eb0b7-1898-53ba-8af4-976cc209b7d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(1+x)arccotx}{x(1+{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282806} {:answer/id #uuid "16de84a4-86fc-59e1-9c76-d990cd8d9808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{arccotx}{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282807} {:answer/id #uuid "c82dc217-0b90-5c97-9d00-b7d02371e170" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{2}+arccotx}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59c8c876-3df0-5ae5-8f0f-2934903b1a53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+(1+{x}^{2})arccotx}{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282805} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a388b08-6722-5f90-a867-d244b4e63021" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1330ca8f-a471-5b0b-b8f9-0e720b30433b" :question/math-academy-id "q-73447" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{arccotx}{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we let $u(x)=arccotx$ and $v(x)=x$, and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{and}\\,{v}^{′}(x)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\cdot x-arccotx\\cdot 1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\frac{x}{1+{x}^{2}}-arccotx}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(\\frac{x+(1+{x}^{2})arccotx}{1+{x}^{2}})}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{x+(1+{x}^{2})arccotx}{{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282809 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20a5f15e-8a26-57af-a867-8f8ae02a91c1" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c114d124-80ce-52d9-8bc9-2c3bc5d9d371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{3x}|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-\\frac{{e}^{3x}arccscx}{{e}^{3x}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282811} {:answer/id #uuid "b1447c01-6127-53b1-a263-67011d1a8c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{({e}^{3x}-1)|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-\\frac{3{e}^{3x}arccscx}{({e}^{3x}-1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282812} {:answer/id #uuid "7539412d-3395-5d5b-8cca-d8405ca607cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{({e}^{3x}-1)|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+\\frac{{e}^{3x}arccscx}{({e}^{3x}-1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282813} {:answer/id #uuid "4c69394d-ba49-5db4-9dcd-c2d8fe49f3b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{3x}-1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+\\frac{3arccscx}{{e}^{3x}({e}^{3x}-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282814} {:answer/id #uuid "e83104c7-623e-5886-a5cc-1bed3169ad1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{{e}^{3x}|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+\\frac{{e}^{3x}arccscx}{{e}^{3x}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1447c01-6127-53b1-a263-67011d1a8c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{({e}^{3x}-1)|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-\\frac{3{e}^{3x}arccscx}{({e}^{3x}-1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282812} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc6284af-6aec-5a92-b699-6042567571b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1cfa91c9-7c5b-5810-b341-38bc9862e893" :question/math-academy-id "q-73448" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{arccscx}{{e}^{3x}-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we let $u(x)=arccscx$ and $v(x)={e}^{3x}-1$, and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{and}\\,{v}^{′}(x)=3{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\cdot ({e}^{3x}-1)-arccscx\\cdot 3{e}^{3x}}{({e}^{3x}-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{({e}^{3x}-1)|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}-\\frac{3{e}^{3x}arccscx}{({e}^{3x}-1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
